<title>UK: Saudi cuts June Extra Lt crude to U.S., others fla.</title>
<headline>Saudi cuts June Extra Lt crude to U.S., others fla.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saudi Aramco has cut the price of its Berri Extra Light crude for U.S. customers in June but left most other grades unchanged, traders said on Monday.</p>
<p>Berri Extra Light would be priced at WTI -$2.70 a barrel, down from WTI -$2.70 in May, they said.  </p>
<p>The state oil giant left the prices of its Arab Light and Arab Heavy crudes unchanged at WTI -$3.60 and WTI -$5.50 a barrel respectively, they said.</p>
<p>The price of Arab Medium crude in June for U.S. customers was not immediately available.</p>
<p>--Mark Thompson, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7930</p>
</text>
